  "summary": "ESCAPE-MeVO randomized 530 patients with medium-vessel ischemic stroke and favorable imaging within 12 hours to EVT plus usual care or usual care alone. Excellent 90-day outcome occurred in 41.6% versus 43.1% (adjusted rate ratio 0.95; 95% CI 0.79–1.15). Mortality and symptomatic intracranial hemorrhage were numerically higher with EVT.",
  "whyItMatters": "Routine thrombectomy for this medium-vessel population was not supported. The result should inform stroke-center transfer discussions without delaying assessment for established reperfusion indications.",
  "limitations": "Open-label treatment with blinded outcomes; 84.7% had MCA-branch occlusions. The trial does not exclude benefit in an unidentified subgroup or address all future devices.",
  "population": "Imaging-selected medium-vessel occlusion stroke within 12 hours in five countries.",
  "sampleSize": 530,
  "intervention": "EVT plus usual care.",
  "comparator": "Usual care alone.",
  "primaryEndpoint": "Modified Rankin Scale 0–1 at 90 days.",
  "findings": [
    "Mortality: 13.3% versus 8.4%; adjusted HR 1.82 (95% CI 1.06–3.12).",
    "Symptomatic intracranial hemorrhage: 5.4% versus 2.2%."
  ],
